      "content": "Fair enough, you're sticking to the legal theory. But let's get real for a second—if we keep applying this extremely high bar of 'incontrovertible proof' to every political scandal, doesn't that essentially grant immunity to anyone powerful enough to coordinate a cover-up? \n\nIf a group of people all swear they saw the same thing, and the only reason we can't convict is because there isn't a 'smoking gun' email or a video recording, isn't that just a failure of our legal system to adapt to modern reality? It feels like you're suggesting that as long as a conspiracy is well-executed, it's legally indistinguishable from innocence. Don't you think the sheer weight of many consistent testimonies should effectively tip the scale of truth?",
